    "UC-A5": {
      "name": "Credential-based privilege escalation",
      "description": "Escalate from a low-privilege account to higher privileges using credential and OS mechanics.",
      "detail": "Starting from an initial foothold, the attacker escalates to domain admin by stealing credentials and moving laterally through Active Directory trust relationships. This is the financial/ransomware-operator pattern: the realistic goal is to reach the target privilege level by the shortest and quietest path through the identity layer: Kerberos and NTLM exchanges, session tokens, group memberships, and misconfigured ACLs. It is demanding on service, operating-system, identity, action, and observation fidelity, which is why real-software environments support it well while abstract simulators do not.",
